Runs 1 to 4: the body runs inside the lock and unlock! also follows a failed body; NoWait on a busy item gives Busy with no body and no unlock; Wait on a busy item tries NoWait first, prints
"waiting for another tln: <item>" once to stderr, then takes the lock with Wait.
Runs 5 to 7: the project file is recorded under the lock of projects.json (nowait first). The lock holder deletes the stale temp of the item (R-CC2). A temp copy is never recorded (R-PD11).
No files: no Fx call. Only a skipped file: the lock and the read, and no write. No ask! call runs under a lock (the fake would log a VIOLATION line).
